<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhimavaram</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhimavaram is a town in the Godavari delta of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It is known for the Somarama temple, one of the five Pancharama shrines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>, built under the Eastern Chalukya kings. It is now a centre of aquaculture and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhimavaram.jpg" alt="Bhimavaram" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: iMahesh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Bhimavaram_Shiva_temple_Galigopuram.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
